From f387acdede9b0be3938e22dcf749e5ed9c1dccb1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:59:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 234/241] trans: a vtable entry whose method bounds fail for
 the type is null

fend-core 1.5.8 makes a `dyn Iterator` of `Skip<BihomographicIterator>`
(no TrustedRandomAccess). The vtable lists libcore's hidden

    unsafe fn __iterator_get_unchecked(&mut self, idx: usize) -> Self::Item
    where Self: TrustedRandomAccessNoCoerce

(vtable.cpp leaves out only `where Self: Sized` methods), and Trans
Enumerate monomorphised Skip's override for it. That body reads
`Self::MAY_HAVE_SIDE_EFFECT`; `Skip<I>: TrustedRandomAccessNoCoerce`
needs `I: ..`, so no impl applies and get_value falls back to the trait's
required const. Deserialised, that const is `Generic` with no MIR, and
enumerate dereferenced the null MIR pointer:

    terminate called after throwing an instance of 'char const*'

rustc leaves such an entry vacant (impossible predicates): the trait
object can't satisfy the bound, so the entry is never called. The
trait-provided-method check of public impls already tested a method's
bounds; it is now Trans_Enumerate_BoundsHold, and
Trans_Enumerate_VTableMethodPresent applies it to vtable entries in all
three places that walk them: enumeration, the cleanup re-run's stub
list, and Trans_AutoImpls, which writes a null pointer for the entry.

A `Generic` constant without MIR now hits a BUG naming the path instead
of the bare throw.

Upstream bug: any `Box<dyn Iterator>` of `.skip(n)` over an iterator
without TrustedRandomAccess hit it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
