+/// Whether `type`'s vtable for a trait points at trait method `fcn` (of `trait_path`, monomorphised): not when the
+/// method's own where-clauses fail for the type, e.g. Iterator's `__iterator_get_unchecked` (`where Self:
+/// TrustedRandomAccessNoCoerce`) for `Skip<I>` over a plain iterator. rustc leaves such an entry null: the trait object
+/// can't call it, and the method's body may not even resolve for that type.
+extern bool Trans_Enumerate_VTableMethodPresent(const StaticTraitResolve& resolve, const ::HIR::TypeRef& type, const ::HIR::GenericPath& trait_path, const ::HIR::Function& fcn);
 
